%erg 0.1
Title: STATE Status block stops storing ticket counts
Created: 2026-10-19
Author: Minh Ha-Duong

--- log ---
2026-10-19T19:51Z Minh Ha-Duong created

--- body ---
## Context
`scripts/refresh-STATE.py` (run by `/lair`) writes ticket counts, "next"
picks and recent commits into the tracked `## Status` block of STATE.md
(`rules/state.md`). Every PR that closes or unblocks a ticket makes those
numbers stale on merge, and every parallel PR then touches the same lines.

Incident, sen-causal-reading, 2026-10-19: PR #20 (close of 0025) was sent
back by `/verify-gate` (REROLL, round 1) for one reason only, STATE.md:38
still reading "18 open · 8 ready" instead of 17/7. The gate cited the 0007
close commit f2df2c8, which had hand-edited that line, as precedent; the
simplify seat said the block is generated and must not be hand-edited.
Reviewers disagree, and each ticket close costs a review round over a
number a script computes in milliseconds.

## Decision (author, 2026-10-19)
Option 1: STATE.md stops storing derived counts. Live numbers come from
`erg ready tickets/`, `erg list` and `/dashboard` when needed. STATE keeps
what only a human writes (blockers, decisions, next actions in prose).

## Design notes
- STATE.md is injected at session start by a hook (`rules/state.md`).
  Preferred shape: the hook (or `refresh-STATE.py --print`) computes the
  counts and appends them to the injected context at read time, so sessions
  still see the numbers without any committed copy.
- Volatile items to drop from the committed block: open/ready counts,
  awaiting-author and next picks, open MRs and CI verdict, last commits.
  A pointer line to the commands replaces them. Decide whether the
  `state-metrics` extension point is also read-time.
- Before removing lines, grep the harness for readers of the block
  (`/yawn` docs-freshness check, `/perch`, `/lair`, `tests/test_refresh_state.py`).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `refresh-STATE.py` no longer writes ticket counts, next picks, MRs or commits into STATE.md
- [ ] Session start still shows live ticket counts, computed at read time
- [ ] `rules/state.md` and `/lair` describe the new contract; `/yawn` no longer flags count drift
- [ ] Tests updated; `make check` passes
- [ ] A ticket-closing PR in a project repo needs no STATE.md edit to pass review
